=3D"corner-intro">A collection of web design and development news and thoug=
hts from CodePen's own Chris Coyier.</p>=0D=0A                          </m=
j-raw>=0D=0A                          <p>Maybe I=E2=80=99m just old (<em>co=
ughs dust</em>), but if you can make a click <em>do something</em> in HTML =
and CSS alone, it always feels cool and fancy to me. Even just =E2=80=9Ccli=
ck to go to another page=E2=80=9D, the foundation of the web, is cool and f=
ancy. And if it happens to go to a same-domain URL, you can animate it, whi=
ch so happens to be <a href=3D"https://post.spmailtechnol.com/f/a/HaEKcvin-=
190XrybblB3zw~~/AABEfhA~/yEnjBtIecWAMwGsUZefYZ_kio9zPjbRDo5yI9jZlkZFCl6I7JK=
kv8bhtbqVUTxXDPDqGqSfzZ3FI9SKTRy2zAIA5-yJHY6a-8aVZCgTBzi9qYrG8mXZkAMexJC8RN=
NBXHxHQeOwb6WBpzHJZj8sd9Q~~">the subject of our CodePen Challenge this past=
 week</a>. </p>=0D=0A=0D=0A<p>Perhaps the first =E2=80=9Ctrick=E2=80=9D for=
 click-something-do-something in HTML+CSS was <a href=3D"https://post.spmai=
ltechnol.com/f/a/AgD7Bbd1IO3fcxx26In54g~~/AABEfhA~/yEnjBtIecWAMwGsUZefYZ0_l=
FTcgu6Zck4l0-i3gr2-ZLxLI8Zg-FOEff28ktYfcANFiGfebbspNQMfzzXMfDWwvNUxO6x03pE1=
zL9xEno_oC-21eFSqn9R3ReHaODTxrc5AUWUnkwJh9kJzAdl6Yg~~">The Checkbox Hack</a=
>, where we could style based on the <code>input:checked ~ .something-else<=
/code> style selector. With this <em>tiny bit</em> of interactive state, pe=
ople built <a href=3D"https://post.spmailtechnol.com/f/a/pKABIPVeajmBc3dlwj=
B07A~~/AABEfhA~/yEnjBtIecWAMwGsUZefYZwbWKJQGbZylZVpOdjGQrDhLp9J96OuJemE6JpE=
s6V-38RhBQjTP0lRNjUF2fZRIytSUUpUrjVyAm-34zSqg3yKJzXEgiSkATaz2NlhlELAJz2yfhr=
Ucmdcw071mHhIc4Q~~">incredible things</a>.</p>=0D=0A=0D=0A<p>But a lot has =
changed since then. Even just <code>&lt;details&gt;</code> came along and g=
ave us an open/closed state with a click, which you can also select off of =
in CSS. </p>=0D=0A=0D=0A<p>Heck, we can <a href=3D"https://post.spmailtechn=
ol.com/f/a/sf90Y2GWFO7rtIWpDJhJ9Q~~/AABEfhA~/GloQxRmeSf8dYD28NIU-iZZf4bc5Yr=
Tjv5HHEEc0_XhovPUsiL35PS9bszCMturfuB98QBDuIOb10XAAYAK--uw5vc_N1xlNLbQ6mBz9z=
Hsr-yHmiF6L3wJeTx92AboSMliiPWHrUvZ4O91Yi6IR2Q~~">use an =E2=80=9Cinvoker=E2=
=80=9D to open a dang anchored popover</a> with a trivial amount of code.</=
p>=0D=0A=0D=0A<p>Or that we can pop a <code>::scroll-button</code> on a scr=
olling container and get a literal clickable button that scrolls the area=
=3F What=3F=3F Check out my <a href=3D"https://post.spmailtechnol.com/f/a/_=
NgqLRWmTU2k28PXOM-rMQ~~/AABEfhA~/1KeQLrEgqZIT6HtXr0RseF5M442zSdrQ3IHVtxMgs7=
_D4OOuxh1dmGjs3_E8vEyhnTNeGck4HRIbznXqVHtj-FvUXYpCoQBNljftrVEcb3D265bryyPcE=
QxlLWDmxJjvJtDwBRcbcvO0pglnbKtZEYW0OMeCLTT_VdjawQqHTx9VffkhF1nS3-omGREeeOmz=
">quantity query carousel</a> for an example there.</p>=0D=0A=0D=0A<p>It=E2=
=80=99s just not that hard anymore to get click-something-do-something acti=
on out of HTML and CSS alone. Here are a few more examples I=E2=80=99ve col=
lected recently.</p>=0D=0A=0D=0A<ul>=0D=0A<li><a href=3D"https://post.spmai=
ltechnol.com/f/a/lb-HNgBWM0JbvbwyBOotzw~~/AABEfhA~/LgNP38lPAEQM39XjGkDLClx4=
-gsUWAidINvp9mYgsuuHABDhfkgMwgGk9NBcXpvtdEGSBZ2Rn7bos5OjB-zJdt4reNjx4u-0dmE=
